---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/use-cases/holiday-gifting";
const title = "Holiday gifting email for Shopify";
const desc = "Guide a buyer from choosing a suitable gift to a truthful fulfillment option. Keep the buyer and recipient distinct, and derive urgency from the store\u2019s actual preparation and delivery constraints.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does a different shipping address prove gift intent?",
    "answer": "No. Treat it as uncertain unless supported by an explicit gift choice or other reliable order-level evidence."
  },
  {
    "question": "When should deadline reminders start?",
    "answer": "Work backward from verified product preparation and destination-specific service limits, with enough time for the buyer\u2019s decision. There is no universal holiday schedule."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should a gift recipient receive marketing automatically?",
    "answer": "No. A delivery address is not a marketing signup. Keep buyer service distinct from recipient preferences and voluntary registration."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Workflow playbook</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Capture gift intent without guessing identity</h2>
    <p>Prefer an explicit gift selection, gift message or buyer preference. A different billing and shipping address is a clue, not proof of a gift. Keep unknown orders in an unknown branch, and store intent on the relevant order rather than permanently labeling the customer as a gifter. One person can buy for themselves and for someone else in the same season.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Curate gifts around a real decision</h2>
    <p>Organize by useful constraints such as recipient interests, budget, sizing uncertainty, suitability and packaging. Explain what a bundle contains and which components can be substituted. Food gifts may need ingredient and storage details; custom jewelry may need a consultation before ordering. Match creative to those decisions instead of assuming every buyer is less price-sensitive.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Build the deadline register with fulfillment</h2>
    <p>For each destination, shipping service and product class record production time, dispatch cutoff, timezone, delivery estimate, evidence source and last verification. Custom work and corporate orders need different lead times from stocked goods. The warehouse or fulfillment owner must approve the store-specific promise; a carrier date alone does not account for the store’s preparation queue.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Change urgency when the available service changes</h2>
    <p>Schedule inspiration, comparison and deadline messages around the verified buying window rather than fixed days before a holiday. Re-evaluate queued copy when capacity or service availability changes. After the standard option closes, show another method only where it is actually available. If arrival cannot be promised, state the remaining option plainly and remove contradictory countdowns.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Check complete bundles and packaging</h2>
    <p>Validate sellable components, gift wrap, gift notes and any required accessories before featuring a bundle. Decide whether partial availability blocks the promotion or permits a clearly described substitute. Align email images and landing-page contents with the fulfilled package. Never silently replace an unavailable gift with a materially different item to keep a deadline campaign running.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Give digital gifts their own fulfillment path</h2>
    <p>Before advertising fast delivery, rehearse payment review, issuance, scheduling, destination address and resend handling. Explain who receives the gift and when. Provide support instructions for an undelivered message without exposing redemption details to the wrong person. A digital format does not by itself establish instantaneous delivery or a physical-product margin comparison.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Keep buyer service separate from recipient marketing</h2>
    <p>Send order support and gift receipts to the appropriate buyer contact. Do not enroll the shipping recipient into marketing merely because their address appears on an order. Let recipients choose whether to register or request care information. Avoid revealing a surprise through unsolicited recipient messaging, and do not assume the buyer personally consumed the gift when scheduling replenishment.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Coordinate offers, returns and corporate inquiries</h2>
    <p>Use the same offer register as other campaigns so gift creative does not accidentally add another discount. State the actual return and exchange terms, including who can request them and how gift receipts work. Route bulk inquiries to an owner who can confirm quantities, addresses and production slots. A previous corporate order is not evidence that a consumer shipping deadline applies again.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Measure the season through fulfillment and redemption</h2>
    <p>Separate known gift orders, self-purchases and unknown intent. Track promised versus actual dispatch, delivery complaints, exchanges and refunds alongside orders attributed to emails. Record gift-card issuance and redemption separately; do not count both as two independent product sales or treat the face value as immediate profit. Compare equal-age cohorts after the return window rather than declaring success from December receipts alone.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Rehearse a cutoff change before peak</h2>
    <p>Proposed exercise: create a mixed physical-and-digital gift order, a destination past cutoff, a missing bundle component and a buyer who also has a self-purchase. Move the shipping cutoff after a message is queued and inspect the final copy. Test supplier event fields and cancellation behavior with these cases. Keep a pause owner, corrected-copy plan and support handoff; retain the verified calendar as a historical record, then revalidate it for the next occasion.</p>
  </div></section>
  <nav class="container pb-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4" aria-label="Related workflows"><a class="link" href="/use-cases/black-friday">Sale calendar</a><a class="link" href="/use-cases/discount-strategy">Offer coordination</a><a class="link" href="/use-cases/email-design">Message rendering</a></nav>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
